Silence...says nothing...
Does silence say nothing?
Yes, literaly, silence says nothing, but it has more power than any word could hold.
Power to hide the pain.
Power to calm a blasting situation.
Power to hold the anger.
Power to reduce the stress.
Power to keep your enemies in their limits.
Power to keep them wondering about your plans.
Power to keep their mouths shut.
Power to hold your reaction in vulnarable situations.
Power to keep you safe from your own temper.
Power to ignore the noise & power to noise up their minds.
And keeping silent when you are angry gives you power & time to overcome the destructive reactions and think about the situation
with your mind and not with the momentary feelings of temper.
It gives you time to solve the problem, not just reacting on it.
It gives you patience to think, not just respond.
It gives a direction to your anger instead of fuel.
It shifts the power from destruction to solution.
It moves the fingers from you to them.
It rotates the table from anger to wisdom.



